{
  "slug": "memstack",
  "name": "Memstack",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "100 battle-tested skills for Claude Code across 10 categories: session memory, git workflows, database migrations, security scanning, deployments, API development, frontend, content/marketing, business docs, and DevOps. Auto-trigger commands fire based on what you're working on. Session handoffs preserve context across conversations. One install deploys across all your projects. 77 free skills included, 23 Pro-exclusive available at memstack.pro.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **18 skills**, **2 commands** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (18): `compress` (Use when the user says 'tokenstack', 'compression', 'token savings', 'proxy status', or asks about context window usage), `diary` (Use when the user says 'save diary', 'log session', 'wrapping up', or at end of a productive session), `echo` (Use when the user references past sessions, asks 'what did we do', 'do you remember', 'last session', 'recall',…), `familiar` (Use when the user says 'dispatch', 'send familiar', 'split task', or needs work split across parallel CC sessions), `forge` (Use when the user says 'forge this', 'new skill', 'create enchantment', or wants to create a MemStack skill), `goal` (Use when the user says 'goal', 'set a goal', 'define the goal', 'plan this properly', or starts a…), `governor` (Use when the user says 'new project', 'project init', 'what tier', 'scope', or discusses project maturity, complexity budget,…), `grimoire` (Use when the user says 'update context', 'update claude', 'save library', or after significant project changes), and 10 more\n- **Commands** (2): `memstack-headroom`, `memstack-search`\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionStart`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install memstack@claude-community` from `cwinvestments/memstack`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 18,
    "hook": 1,
    "command": 2
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
